    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Clinical-Professor-of-Nursing_JR100681": {
      "title": "Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking two qualified applicants for Assistant Clinical Professor of Nursing positions. The standard teaching load is 12 course credit hours per semester or 24 credits over an academic year. This position seeks candidates with at least two years of medical-surgical and/or critical care nursing expertise. Experience in critical care settings, such as ICU, Emergency Department, or Telemetry, is highly preferred. This position carries ongoing responsibility for curriculum development, planning, teaching, guiding, monitoring, and evaluating student learning in the classroom and clinical practice settings to support continuous improvement of courses and clinical experiences. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Willi ngness   to teach   across nursing programs   based on departmental needs .   Teaching theor y, laboratory, and /or   clinical   components   in nursing education program s .   Teaching   and evaluating assigned courses.    Supervising student performance of clinical skills in the lab and/or clinical setting s ( clinical faculty -to- student ratio is not more than 1:10 ) .   Promot ing   positive and productive relationships with service are a   hospitals, clinics, and agencies .   Participat ing   in   program, department, and university   assessment   and accreditation   activities.     Participat ing   in academic advising and guidance of students   Attend ing   p rogram and   d epartment faculty meetings.    Providing students   with   a   detailed course   syllabus   in writing,   following CMU   Nursing guidelines   and timelines .   Establishing, posting, and keeping a minimum of five office hours weekly over four days during each term of the academic year.    Establishing   necessary   procedures to   ensure   that adequate and   accurate   records of student performance are   maintained .   Developing and   maintaining :   An active scholarship   portfolio   ( for t enure-track Assistant Professor), or   Ongoing professional productivity and clinical   expertise   (Assistant Clinical Professor)   Provid ing   service to the   program, department,   university ,   and external community.    Participat ing   in program, department, and university events including commencement.   Maintaining   t imely   and satisfactory performance of responsibilities specified in the faculty member’s employment agreement and CMU Professional Employee Handbook.    ​ Salary: $60,000-$70,000 (master’s prepared); $70,000-$80,000 (doctoral prepared) Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! EDUCATION   AND   EXPERIENCE:       Required   Qualifications   E ligible for or hold ing   a current license in   good standing   to practice as a Registered Nurse in Colorado .     Minimum of   two years of   full-time   professional clinical   nursing   experience , with preference given to candidates with experience in critical care settings (ICU, ED, Telemetry)     Graduate degree in   n ursing   from a   national accredited school of nursing.    Demonstrate knowledge and skills related to :   Adult learning principles   Teaching   methodology   C urriculum development and evaluation   O r a written plan for obtaining such knowledge   beginning no later than the first year of teaching.     LANGUAGE SKILLS   Ability to read, analyze, and interpret   professional journals, technical procedures, and governmental regulations. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from   students, colleagues, and community partners.      MATHEMATICAL SKILLS   Ability to apply basic mathematical concepts such as fractions, percentages,   ratios   and proportions to practic e   situations.     REASONING ABILITY   Ability to define problems, collect   and analyze   data,   establish   facts, and draw valid conclusions.     PHYSICAL DEMANDS   The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable   accommodation   may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.   While performing the duties of this job, the employee is   frequently   required to stand, walk, sit, and talk, or hear. The employee must occasionally lift and/move up to 10 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include clos e,   distance   and   peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust   focus .     WORK ENVIRONMENT   The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job. Reasonable   accommodation   may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in office, classroom, and clinical settings. The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day.     DEADLINE :   To ensure consideration, complete applications should be received   by  October 15, 2026. DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Jodi Noga, jnoga@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
