    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-Master-of-Science-in-Occupational-Therapy_JR100562": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor/Clinical Professor for Master of Science in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-14\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor for the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program with practice mastery in physical rehabilitation. This is a full-time tenure-track or clinical-track, 12-month position with a start date of January 6, 2027. The standard academic load is 18-20 credit hours per year on site. Participation in scholarship, advising, and service to the program, department, and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach graduate-level courses within the Master of Science in Occupational Therapy Program. Develop and coordinate course design, course delivery, and participate in the evaluation of didactic and clinical curriculum. Advise and mentor graduate students, including guiding faculty-led research projects Initiate an ongoing scholarly agenda in area of expertise. Ongoing development and evaluation of curriculum to align with program goals and accreditation standards. Support admissions and applicant screening processes Complete professional development activities and service to the Department, University and community. Participate in ACOTE accreditation, and program/University assessment processes. Perform other program and department level duties as assigned. Salary: $95,000-$100,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty and responsibility satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required.  EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE:  Minimum Qualifications Required:  EITHER A) Occupational therapist with the following: Master's degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program AND currently pursuing a Doctoral degree, or entry-level Doctoral degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. OR B) Post-professional OTD/DOT degree from an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Must have certification from the National Board for Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT). Licensed or eligible for licensure as an occupational therapist in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. All candidates should possess excellent communication, interpersonal, and leadership skills. Detail-oriented with strong organizational, critical thinking, and problem-solving abilities. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Preferred Qualifications: Clinical experience in adult physical rehabilitation. Previous academic teaching experience. Clinical teaching experience as a Level II Fieldwork educator. Evidence of scholarship (presentations, articles, posters, etc.). Active in community service and participation Leadership in local, regional, or national occupational therapy associations An earned terminal doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline (PhD, EdD). Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with adults in physical rehabilitation settings, working with students from diverse backgrounds, and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Deadline: This position will remain open until filled. Applications received by 9/15 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. How to Apply : Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact: Sarah Gray, search Chair at: sgray2@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Tech-Grand-Junction-CO/Technical-Instructor-of-Medical-Office-Assisting_JR100467": {
      "title": "Technical Instructor of Medical Office Assisting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: We are seeking a passionate and experienced Medical Assistant Instructor to join our faculty. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in medical assisting and a dedication to teaching and mentoring students. As a Medical Assistant Instructor, you will be responsible for delivering high-quality instruction, developing curriculum, and ensuring that students acquire the skills and knowledge necessary to excel in the medical field. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Conduct both lecture and lab instruction for 15 credit hours per semester and maintain 5 hours of office time per week for student consultation and support Work independently and collaboratively with colleagues to develop innovative curriculum that addresses the needs of our diverse student population. Demonstrate extensive knowledge and experience in medical assisting, utilizing the most current equipment and technology to enhance instruction in clinical and administrative procedures. Working knowledge and skill of up-to-date medical assisting principles, methods, and techniques. Evaluate student performance in coursework using industry-related standards and expectations to ensure competency and readiness for the workforce. Determine program needs and manage the program budget, including purchasing and cost control, to maintain high-quality educational resources. Maintain knowledge of industry-standard medical equipment and demonstrate its functionality in instructional settings. Engage successfully with students, healthcare professionals, other educators, and the public in a professional and courteous manner. Assist in the recruitment, advisement, placement, and development of cooperative work experience opportunities for students, and conduct follow-up with graduates. Serve as a representative of the department by participating in committees, task forces, and events at the campus, college, and/or state levels. Exhibit excellent organizational, communication, and presentation skills, along with a positive and enthusiastic attitude towards teaching and student success Excellent organization, communication, and presentation skills. Positive and enthusiastic attitude. Advise students, maintain student files and paperwork, including job sheets, registration, and intent to graduate. Coordinate industry engagement with local employers for advisory committee, internship, and other industry specific needs. Perform all responsibilities and instructional duties in accordance with local, state, and federal regulations as well as CMU Tech/CMU policies and procedures. Ensure the maintenance of appropriate approvals & accreditation, maintain and develop the curriculum in step with industry and state requirements. Promote a positive collegiate atmosphere and develop positive relationships with students, faculty, and staff. Applicant will perform other duties as required. Salary: $53,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! QUALIFICATIONS: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE Minimum Qualifications Required: Minimum of 4,000 hours of w ork experience as a Medical Assistant in a clinical setting within the last five years. Preferred Qualifications: Associate degree or higher in related field Certified Medical Assistant (CMA) or Registered Medical Assistant (RMA) credentials. Evidence of teaching ability and or previous teaching experience in field COMPUTER SKILLS Ability to utilize PowerPoint, Learning Management System technology to maintain grades and content. LANGUAGE SKILLS Ability to read, analyze, and interpret general business periodicals, professional journals, technical procedures and governmental regulations.  Ability to write reports, business correspondence and procedure manuals.  Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from groups of managers, clients, customers and the public. MATHEMATICAL SKILLS Ability to apply accounting models and mathematical concepts such as probability and statistical inference.  Ability to apply concepts such as fractions, percentages, ratios and proportions to practical situations. REASONING ABILITY Ability to define problems, collect data, establish facts, and draw valid conclusions. Ability to interpret an extensive variety of technical instructions in mathematical or diagram form, to interpret an extensive variety of legal and regulatory documents and deal with several abstract and concrete variables. PHYSICAL DEMANDS  The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is frequently required to stand, walk, sit, and talk or hear.  The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 40 pounds.  Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and ability to adjust focus. WORK ENVIRONMENT  The work environment characteristics described here are representative of those an employee encounters while performing the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The employee typically performs the duties of the job in an open office setting.  The noise level in the work environment is moderate to loud at times, with several disruptions throughout the day. This position will remain open until filled. Applications received by 9/1 will receive priority consideration, and applications received after that date will be reviewed on a weekly basis until the position is filled. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Kinesiology_JR100111": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Kinesiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-22\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: CMU encourages students to engage in a healthy campus lifestyle. As part of our campus-wide Health and Wellness program, every student takes the Health & Wellness course and at least one activity class (and most take three or more) to meet graduation requirements for all undergraduate degrees. Our activity classes range from Aerobics to Zumba and we are always looking for local instructors who are highly experienced in the courses we offer. With the great community of health, fitness, and wellness experts we enjoy in Western Colorado, YOU could be a great fit to educate our Mavericks! Please explore the list below to see our full list of course offerings. If you see an activity you are trained in and passionate about, we encourage you to apply and join the Maverick family! List of Activity Courses: Beginning Swimming, Intermediate Swimming, Springboard Diving, Water Polo, Rock Climbing, Hiking, Beginning Golf, Intermediate Golf, Disc Golf and Ultimate Frisbee, Badminton, Karate, Beginning Tennis, Pickleball, Racquet Sports, Fitness Walking, Physical Conditioning, Intermediate Weight Training, Weight Training, Aerobics, Step Aerobics, Self-Defense, Pilates, Indoor Cycling, Adaptive Physical Activity, Introduction to Yoga, Hatha Yoga Relaxation, Flow Yoga, Zumba, Snorkeling/Free Diving, and Social Dance. In addition to our activity classes, we are also looking for instructors who may be interested and qualified to teach the Health & Wellness course. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teaching as an Adjunct Lecturer at CMU requires familiarity and use of our online learning platform, D2L, along with the ability to create a syllabus with engaging and educating methodologies to assess student learning.  Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. ‌ Minimum Qualifications Required: Bachelor’s degree or higher or we will consider accredited certification in your activity and/or 5 years of documented experienced teaching.  Master's degree is required to teach KINE 100 Health and Wellness How to Apply : Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Direct Inquiries Contact:  Kristin Heumann, kheumann@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Lecturer-of-Business_JR100078": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-06\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking applications for a part-time in-person Lecturer of Economics. The ideal candidates would have experience teaching Economics principles courses. Part-time faculty at CMU are part-time employees who are hired on an as-needed basis. This job ad is to collect applications for qualified lecturers but communication to applicants may be delayed as faculty needs fluctuate. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. This position will consist of teaching one to two 3-credit hour courses per semester, starting fall 2026 (mid-August). Courses taught will be primarily the 200-level Principles of Microeconomics and/or Principles of Macroeconomics courses the first semester with options to teach upper-level economics courses in the future depending on experience. In addition, the Lecturer must hold a minimum of two office hours weekly for one course, plus a minimum of one office hour for each additional course, up to a maximum of five office hours per week. Salary: $600.00 - $850.00 per credit hour. Adjunct faculty are pair on a per credit hour basis, commensurate with education ad experience. ‌ Minimum Qualifications Required:  Masters degree in Economics or closely-related discipline with at least 18 graduate level credit hours in Economics. Preferred Qualifications: PhD preferred but not required. How to Apply:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a:  Cover letter  Resume  Include the name, phone number, email address and relationship of at least three professional references who can attest to your ability to perform the job you are applying for. Professional references should include at least one current or former supervisor.  Professional reference may also include current or former employers, colleagues or other professionals who have first-hand knowledge and can recommend you for employment.  Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire) ​ Direct Inquiries Contact:  Suzanne Owens-Ott; sowens@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
