    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Clinical-Professor-for-the-Bechtel-Physician-Assistant-Program_JR100294": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor/Clinical Professor for the Bechtel Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor to teach in the Bechtel Physician Assistant Program. This is a full-time, in person tenure or clinical track, 12-month position. Courses may be assigned as in-person, or hybrid. Professional development in the discipline, involvement with advising, and service to the department and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Develop and coordinate course design, course delivery, and participate in the evaluation of didactic and clinical curriculum. Participate in the admissions process and the applicant screening process. Teach assigned courses in the PA program. Provide student academic advising and evaluation. Assist in clinical site visits. Participate in ARC-PA accreditation processes and program/university assessment. Complete professional development activities and service to the University and community. Participate in the program's ongoing self-assessment process. Administrative responsibilities as assigned. Salary: $98,000-$100,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! REQUIRED EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE Minimum Qualifications Required: Physician Assistant with the following: Master's degree from an accredited Physician Assistant program. Current certification by the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA). Licensed or eligible for licensure as a Physician Assistant in the State of Colorado. Minimum of two years of clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience. Experience with precepting students. Active in community services and participation/leadership in local, regional, or national Physician Assistant or other medical organizations. An earned academic doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. How to Apply : Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information.  In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume or CV Names and contact information of three (3) professional references Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document.  Official transcripts will be required upon hire) Primary Contact: Rachel Weinzimmer, rweinzimmer@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-Assistant-Program-Director-for-the-Bechtel-Physician-Assistant-Program_JR100759": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor/Assistant Program Director for the Bechtel Physician Assistant Program",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for the position of Assistant Program Director to lead and teach in the Bechtel Physician Assistant Program. This is a full-time, in person, 12-month position, with the option of flipping to the clinical track. Courses may be assigned as in-person, or hybrid. Professional development in the discipline, involvement with advising, and service to the department and profession are expected. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Duties as Assistant Program Director: Assume the role of Interim Program Director in the absence of the Program Director.  Organize and moderate faculty meetings in the absence of the Program Director. Conduct an annual overview of the curriculum to ensure it aligns with the current PANCE blueprint. Oversee course curriculum delivery and maintain syllabi consistent with University and ARC-PA standards.    Make recommendations for curriculum change as needed.  Provide oversight and monitoring of the program’s assessment and evaluation processes. Mentor and onboard new faculty. Review and approve semester schedules. Review and provide guidance on the clinical-year curriculum in partnership with the Medical Director and Director(s) of Clinical Education. Represent the PA program at administrative meetings as deemed appropriate by the Program Director. Assist the Program Director in performing an annual review and update of the student handbook. Assist in the Program’s self-study and accreditation process, ensuring that accreditation standards related to the Program curriculum are appropriately addressed, and assist in compiling and completing documentation for the accreditation process. Oversee the course fee budget Update the program ARC-PA portal as required by the ARC-PA. Participate in preparing documents for accreditation application, self-study, and site visit activities Recruit and advise adjunct faculty Providing leadership and support to didactic students and on-campus faculty Develop and coordinate course design, course delivery, and participate in the evaluation of didactic and clinical curriculum.   Duties as Faculty member: Participate in the admissions process and the applicant screening process. Teach assigned courses in the PA program. Provide student academic advising and evaluation. Assist in clinical site visits. Complete professional development activities and service to the University and community.   REQUIRED EDUCATION and EXPERIENCE   Minimum Qualifications Required: Physician Assistant with the following: Master's degree from an accredited Physician Assistant program. Current certification by the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA). Licensed or eligible for licensure as a Physician Assistant in the State of Colorado. Minimum of three years of full-time higher education experience     Preferred Qualifications: Active in community services and participation/leadership in local, regional, or national Physician Assistant or other medical organizations. An earned academic doctoral degree in an appropriate discipline. Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education.   Salary: $125,000 - $130,000 plus a $5,000 stipend for assistant program director role. Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a:  Cover letter CV Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed. If your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Names and contact information for three references.   Direct Inquiries Contact:  Dan Millward, dmillward@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Geosciences_JR100760": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Geosciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Geosciences specializing in Structural Geology in the Geosciences Program. This is a full-time, tenure-track position starting August 2027. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per fall and spring semester. Scholarship in the discipline, involvement with advising, and service to the university, department, and profession are expected. We encourage applications from candidates whose experience and interests align with the goals of this position, even if they do not meet every preferred qualification. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach geosciences courses and labs at both the introductory and upper-division levels for liberal arts and science majors, including upper-level Structural Geology. Establish a research program in Structural Geology and/or related areas creating meaningful opportunities for undergraduate geoscience majors and geology minors. Other related fields include Geophysics, Planetary Geology, Economic Geology, and/or Energy Transition. Integrate field-based research experiences and geospatial methods into teaching and research, including the application of GIS and/or remote sensing tools. Participate in the department's six-week Geosciences Summer Field Camp, including projects focused on Structural Geology mapping. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Participate in ongoing assessments and improvements of the geosciences program and curriculum. Engage in service to the university, program, department, and profession. Minimum Qualifications Required Ph.D. in Geosciences or a closely related discipline by summer 2027. Demonstrated expertise in Structural Geology. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching and creating a positive learning environment. Enthusiasm for working with and inspiring undergraduate students. Ability and enthusiasm for supervising undergraduate research that actively engages students in solving real-world geoscience problems, integrating geological and geospatial methods with meaningful field-based experiences. Ability to be team-focused, communicate, and work collaboratively and collegially with colleagues. Enthusiasm for supporting a curriculum that integrates field-based, lab-based, and computational approaches to prepare students for careers in both industry and academia.   Preferred Qualifications Enthusiasm for teaching the following: Introductory geosciences courses, including Physical Geology, Natural Hazards, Geology of Colorado, and/or Weather and Climate. Required upper-level Geophysics lecture and lab courses and/or developing new courses related to the candidate’s area of expertise. Interest in teaching courses in GIS including remote sensing. Demonstrated expertise or research interests that complement Structural Geology in one or more of the following areas: Geophysics, Planetary Geology, Economic Geology, and/or Energy Transition. Experience applying GIS and/or remote sensing tools in teaching and research. Research interests that complement or diversify the research of current CMU geosciences faculty and provide meaningful research experiences for undergraduate students. Strong background in field-based instruction and research. Salary: $64,000 - $68,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information!   How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a:  Please be prepared to upload the following materials: Cover Letter (one page): Summarize your qualifications and interest in the position. Curriculum Vitae (CV): Include published papers, manuscripts accepted for publication, proposals submitted and awarded, courses taught, students mentored, awards, and other relevant academic and professional achievements. Statement of Teaching Interests (max. 2 pages) : Describe previous formal teaching experience and future teaching goals; previous undergraduate mentoring contributions and future mentoring goals; and experience and approaches to teaching students from varied educational, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds and levels of preparation, including specific strategies that support belonging, learning, and academic success of all students. Statement of Research Interests (max. 2 pages) : Describe previous research accomplishments and significant scientific contributions; future research goals including plans for developing an independent research program at CMU; previous experience mentoring undergraduate researchers, and plans for involving undergraduate students in future research. Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed: If your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Names and contact information for three references.   Application Deadline:  The search closes on December 14, 2026. To ensure consideration, complete applications must be received by December 13, 2026, at 11:59 PM Mountain Standard Time.   Direct Inquiries Contact:  Dr. Wade Aubin, waubin@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Assistant-Professor-of-Geosciences_JR100761": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Geosciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Geosciences specializing in Hydrology, Geomorphology, and Watershed Science in the Geosciences Program. This is a full-time, tenure-track position starting August 2027. The standard teaching load is 12 credit hours per fall and spring semester. Scholarship in the discipline, involvement with advising, and service to the university, program, department, and profession are expected. We encourage applications from candidates whose experience and interests align with the goals of this position, even if they do not meet every preferred qualification. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. Teach geosciences courses and labs at both the introductory and upper-division levels for liberal arts and science majors; upper-level courses include Hydrology, River Dynamics, Geomorphology, and/or Groundwater. Establish a research program creating meaningful opportunities for undergraduate geoscience majors and watershed science minors within the following research fields: watershed and river processes, critical zone science, climate-driven environmental geohazards, and/or geomorphology. Participate in the department's six-week Geosciences Summer Field Camp, including mapping projects focused on the candidate’s area of expertise. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Participate in ongoing assessments and improvement of the geosciences program and curriculum. Engage in service to the university, program, department, and profession. Minimum Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in Geosciences or a closely related discipline by summer 2027. Demonstrated expertise in Water Resources science. Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching and creating a positive learning environment.  Enthusiasm for working with and inspiring undergraduate students. Ability and enthusiasm for supervising undergraduate research that actively engages students in solving real-world Earth science problems, particularly those focusing on western water resources, and integrating geologic, hydrologic, and geospatial methods with meaningful field-based experiences. Ability to be team-focused, communicate, and work collaboratively and collegially with colleagues. Enthusiasm for supporting a curriculum that integrates field-based, lab-based, and computational approaches to prepare students for careers in both industry and academia.   Preferred Qualifications:   Enthusiasm for teaching the following: Introductory geosciences courses, especially Natural Hazards, Water, People, and Environment, Oceanography, and Weather and Climate. Required upper-level Hydrology and River Dynamics, Geomorphology, and/or Groundwater courses, and/or developing new courses related to the candidate’s area of expertise. Interest in teaching courses in GIS including remote sensing. Demonstrated expertise or research interests in western water resources and/or the upper Colorado River basin in the context of watershed and river processes, critical zone science, climate-driven environmental geohazards, and/or geomorphology. Experience applying GIS and/or remote sensing tools in teaching and research. Research interests that complement and diversify the research of current CMU geosciences faculty and provide meaningful research experiences for undergraduate students. Strong background in field-based instruction and research. Salary: $64,000 - $68,000 Commensurate with education and experience. Excellent health and retirement benefits package: Click here for more information! How to Apply: Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a:  Cover letter (1 page) – Summarize your qualifications and interest in the position. CV: Include published papers, manuscripts accepted for publication, proposals submitted and awarded, classes taught, students mentored, awards, and other relevant academic and professional achievements. Statement of TeachingI (max. 2 pages) : Describe previous formal teaching experience and future teaching goals; previous undergraduate mentoring contributions and future mentoring goals; and experience and approaches to teaching students from varied educational, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds and levels of preparation, including specific strategies that support belonging, learning, and academic success of all students. Statement of Research Interests (max. 2 pages) : Describe previous research accomplishments and significant scientific contributions; future research goals including plans for developing an independent research program at CMU; previous experience mentoring undergraduate researchers, and plans for involving undergraduate students in future research. Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed: If your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading the document. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. Names and contact information for three references.   Application Deadline:  The search closes on December 14, 2026.  To ensure consideration, complete applications must be received by December 13, 2026, at 11:59 PM Mountain Standard Time.   Direct Inquiries Contact:  Dr. Marion McKenzie, mmckenzie2@coloradomesa.edu Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    },
    "https://coloradomesa.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/CMUCareers/job/CMU-Main-Campus-Grand-Junction-CO/Adjunct-Faculty--Lecturer-of-Photography_JR100757": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Lecturer of Photography",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nANNOUNCMENT OF POSITION VACANCY ABOUT THIS POSITION Summary: Colorado Mesa University is seeking applications for a part-time Professor of Photography. The ideal candidates would have experience teaching Photography. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES  include the following. Other related duties may be assigned. This position will consist of teaching two 3-credit hour courses per semester, starting January 2027. Both courses will be our Introduction to Photography course. Introduction to Photography is a 200-level foundations course delivered to majors in all programs of the Art and Design Department. Minimum Qualifications Required: MA or MFA in Photography or other art related field. OR BFA in Photography or related field with a combined minimum of at least 10 years of experience working in an art related field.  Salary: $600-$850 per credit hour. Commensurate with education and experience. ‌ DIRECT INQUIRIES CONTACT: Eric Elliot, eelliott2@coloradomesa.edu HOW TO APPLY:  Applicants will be asked to complete an online application by creating a profile and then providing personal and demographic information. In addition, please be prepared to upload a: Cover letter Resume Copy of transcripts for all degrees completed (if your transcripts include a social security number or birthdate, please redact that information before uploading) Colorado Mesa University is particularly interested in candidates who have experience working with students from diverse backgrounds and who have a demonstrated commitment to improving the levels of access and success for underrepresented students within higher education. Colorado Mesa University is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final applicants being considered for employment. Background investigations include reference checks, a criminal history record check, and when appropriate, a financial and/or motor vehicle history. Applicant must be able to verify U.S. employment eligibility. Colorado Mesa University is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to a culturally diverse faculty, staff and student body. Women and minorities are encouraged to apply. Any person with a disability as defined by the ADA Amendments Act of 2008 (ADAAA) may be provided reasonable accommodation upon request to enable the person to complete an employment assessment. To request an accommodation, please contact the CMU Human Resources Office by phone or email. You may be asked to provide additional information, including medical documentation, regarding functional limitations and the type of accommodation needed."
    }
